        "description": "The morphological post-processor checks the candidate against a PAST_FORMS lookup table but the check occurs after inflection is applied, not before. Irregular verbs whose simple past differs from the '-ed' suffix are returned uninflected, giving the original irregular form instead of the target tense.",
        "fix": "_match_morphology: check candidate base form against PAST_FORMS before inflecting."
      },
      {
        "id": 2,
        "name": "Double-Inflection Bug",
        "count": 1,
        "examples": [
          "procured\u2192eatenned"
        ],
        "description": "When a candidate is already in irregular-past form (e.g. 'eaten') and falls through the PAST_FORMS guard, the inflection step appends '-ed', producing nonsensical forms like 'eatenned'.",
        "fix": "Move PAST_FORMS membership check earlier in the conditional chain in _match_morphology."
      },
      {
        "id": 3,
        "name": "Semantic Drift (Lite Mode)",
        "count": 3,
        "examples": [
          "diverted\u2192treated",
          "perils\u2192places",
          "acquired\u2192assumed"
        ],
        "description": "Without full word-embedding similarity (FastText / GloVe), the engine falls back to WordNet Wu-Palmer similarity, which operates on synset graphs rather than distributional context. This produces candidates that are synset-adjacent but contextually inappropriate.",
        "fix": "Enable full mode with FastText embeddings (4.5 GB) or substitute a lighter model such as GloVe-300d."
      },
